-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- EFFECTIVE DATES OF A DIVISION, AND A SPECIAL CASE FOR A
-- SURVIVOR'S PENSION (regulations 54.2 to 54.4).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 576 to 584.
--
-- A division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place, or is approved, on the last day of the month in which the
-- information (or the application) reaches the Minister (54.2(1)); the earnings are attributed from the first day of the
-- month that follows (54.2(2)). Regulation 54.3 is repealed. Regulation 54.4 lets the Minister act under section 58(7) of
-- the Act where a survivor's pension would prejudice the applicant and a disability pension would not.

§ `Part V -- Effective dates of a division (regulations 54.2 to 54.4)`

§§ `Regulation 54.2 -- effective dates`

-- src:577 | 54.2 (1) For the purposes of the Act,
-- src:578 | (a) the effective date of the taking place of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is the last day of the month in which the information prescribed for the purposes of paragraph 55.1(1)(a) of the Act, and that is listed in subsection 54(2), is received by the Minister; or
-- src:579 | (b) the effective date of the approval of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is the last day of the month in which the application referred to in paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act is received.
@ref Reg 54.2(1)(a) (src:578)
GIVEN `the date the Minister receives the information prescribed for paragraph 55.1(1)(a) of the Act and listed in subsection 54(2)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 54.2(1)(a) — the effective date of the taking place of a division`
    `the date the Minister receives the information prescribed for paragraph 55.1(1)(a) of the Act and listed in subsection 54(2)` MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` `the date the Minister receives the information prescribed for paragraph 55.1(1)(a) of the Act and listed in subsection 54(2)` PLUS (0 MINUS 1)

@ref Reg 54.2(1)(b) (src:579)
GIVEN `the date the Minister receives the application referred to in paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 54.2(1)(b) — the effective date of the approval of a division`
    `the date the Minister receives the application referred to in paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act` MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` `the date the Minister receives the application referred to in paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act` PLUS (0 MINUS 1)

-- src:580 | (2) The effective date of the attribution of pensionable earnings following the division is the first day of the month following the month in which the effective date of the taking place or approval of the division falls.
@ref Reg 54.2(2) (src:580)
GIVEN `the effective date of the taking place or approval of the division` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 54.2(2) — the effective date of the attribution of pensionable earnings following the division`
    `the effective date of the taking place or approval of the division` MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` `the effective date of the taking place or approval of the division`

§§ `Regulation 54.4 -- a special case in calculating a survivor's pension`

-- src:584 | 54.4 For the purposes of subsection 58(7) of the Act, where the applicant would be financially prejudiced on account of payment to the applicant of a survivor’s pension as referred to in subsection 58(6) of the Act and would not be financially prejudiced on account of payment to the applicant of a disability pension pursuant to subsection 58(7) of the Act, the Minister’s powers may be exercised in accordance with subsection 58(7) of the Act.
@ref Reg 54.4 (src:584)
GIVEN `the applicant would be financially prejudiced on account of payment of a survivor's pension as referred to in subsection 58(6) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 58(6) (piece cp3)
      `the applicant would not be financially prejudiced on account of payment of a disability pension pursuant to subsection 58(7) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 58(7) (piece cp3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 54.4 — the Minister's powers may be exercised in accordance with subsection 58(7) of the Act`
    `the applicant would be financially prejudiced on account of payment of a survivor's pension as referred to in subsection 58(6) of the Act`
    `the applicant would not be financially prejudiced on account of payment of a disability pension pursuant to subsection 58(7) of the Act` MEANS
    `the applicant would be financially prejudiced on account of payment of a survivor's pension as referred to in subsection 58(6) of the Act`
        AND `the applicant would not be financially prejudiced on account of payment of a disability pension pursuant to subsection 58(7) of the Act`
